.TH tuhash n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tuhash
.PP
Pure\-Tcl cryptographic digests: \fBSHA\-256\fR, \fBSHA\-1\fR, \fBMD5\fR. Clean\-room implementations of FIPS 180\-4 / RFC 1321, so no tcllib or binary extension is required. All outputs are verified against the standard test vectors.
.SS Commands
.TS
l l.
Command	Result
\fBsha256 data ?\-encoding utf\-8|binary?\fR	hex SHA\-256 of a string
\fBsha1   data ?\-encoding ...?\fR	hex SHA\-1
\fBmd5    data ?\-encoding ...?\fR	hex MD5
\fBsha256File path\fR / \fBsha1File path\fR / \fBmd5File path\fR	digest of a file's bytes
.TE
.PP
\fB\-encoding utf\-8\fR (default) hashes the UTF\-8 bytes of the string, matching what \fBsha256sum\fR/\fBmd5sum\fR produce in a UTF\-8 locale. \fB\-encoding binary\fR treats the argument as raw bytes (each character a byte 0\-255). The \fB*File\fR variants read the exact bytes on disk.
.CS
package require tclutils::tuhash
tuhash::sha256 "abc"          ;# ba7816bf...f20015ad
tuhash::md5    "abc"          ;# 900150983cd24fb0d6963f7d28e17f72
tuhash::sha256File config.tcl ;# digest of the file
.CE
.PP
Errors use \fB{TCLUTILS TUHASH ...}\fR.
